<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">18072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Eight mourners were killed in central Gaza as they buried their dead, when an Israeli drone struck a funeral procession outside a mosque.</s> <s>Since October's ceasefire, health officials count at least one thousand one hundred twenty-seven Palestinians killed... a truce that Israel violates nearly every day.</s> <s>Friday's strikes brought the day's toll to at least twelve, and each name is a life the ceasefire was meant to protect.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>At London's Old Bailey, William Nyerere Plastow — grandson of Tanzania's founding president Julius Nyerere — told jurors he bought equipment for a raid on an arms factory to try to stop the war in Gaza.</s> <s>British prosecutors charge him under terrorism law over Palestine Action's raid on an Israeli-owned Elbit Systems plant in Bristol, and he was held without trial until February.</s> <s>The courtroom has become the place where a state's terror designation meets a defendant's stated conscience.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Across Southeast Asia, choosing a nuclear reactor now means choosing a patron for half a century.</s> <s>Washington and Beijing are both courting Indonesia, Vietnam and the Philippines as they weigh their first plants, because a vendor pick fixes decades of fuel supply and technical dependency.</s> <s>These nations are making a geopolitical bet dressed as an energy decision, in a contest they did not start.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In the coastal town of Caraballeda, thirteen-year-old twins remain buried beneath a collapsed tower after an earthquake, as rescuers dig by hand for lack of machinery.</s> <s><sub alias="the U.N. children's agency">UNICEF</sub> estimates three point nine million children live in Venezuela's quake-hit areas, and the local child-protection office was itself damaged in the disaster.</s> <s>Families keep clawing at the rubble while the state that should reach them is nowhere near.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Sindh has cut funding for its lady health workers by seventy-five percent, their union says, moving the money to a private company with no governing board.</s> <s>These women deliver vaccines, prenatal care and family planning door-to-door in villages the formal health system never reaches, so a three-quarter cut lands hardest on the rural poor.</s> <s>The union is planning province-wide protests, and how austerity travels from a provincial ledger to a village doorstep is the whole story.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The European Union can't decide whether China is a partner or a threat, and its own officials are now pulling in opposite directions.</s> <s>Trade negotiators want to keep talks and green-tech cooperation with Beijing alive, even as a new security framing treats China as a rival, a contradiction that undercuts the bloc's own bargaining.</s> <s>Europe's economy needs the partnership its security posture is built to reject.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>President Zelensky has fired Mykhailo Fedorov, the minister who forced competitive tenders on Ukraine's arms suppliers and cut the country's weapons bill.</s> <s>Fedorov had replaced inflated no-bid contracts that padded politically connected firms, making enemies across the defense sector, and his removal, which sparked protests, looks like that sector winning.</s> <s>The man who saved Ukraine money in wartime was pushed out for it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A twenty-twenty American order that stripped Hong Kong of preferential trade and export treatment has quietly expired, unrenewed.</s> <s>That order followed Beijing's national security law, and letting it lapse restores Hong Kong's access to American markets without any new legislation.</s> <s>China calls it a step toward normal trade, though what Washington intended by simply letting the clock run out remains unspoken.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Forecasters warn this El Niño could rank among the strongest ever recorded, reorganizing rainfall across Africa, South Asia and Latin America months before it strikes.</s> <s>The science arrives early, yet money for smallholder farmers almost always comes after the floods and droughts, not before.</s> <s>Scientists are pressing governments to fund anticipatory action now, because knowing and failing to prepare is a policy failure, not a natural one.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Seven decades of militarized no-man's-land turned the Korean Demilitarized Zone into one of Asia's richest wildlife sanctuaries, and now South Korea is redrawing its buffer for development.</s> <s>That strip shelters globally endangered migratory birds like the red-crowned crane, habitat that peace treaties elsewhere failed to protect.</s> <s>A geopolitical accident created an ecological commons, and easing the border could quietly undo it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A seven point three magnitude earthquake struck about thirty miles off the coast of Chiapas, triggering tsunami warnings across Mexico, Guatemala and El Salvador.</s> <s>The shallow rupture sits on the Cocos-North America subduction boundary, precisely the geometry that produces destructive tsunamis.</s> <s>Coastal residents were told to leave the beaches, waiting to learn whether the sea would answer.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In a Toronto lab, a goldfish picking bowls has kept beating AI chatbots at forecasting the World Cup.</s> <s>Large language models pattern-match plausible stories about players like Mbappé and Messi rather than modelling real probability, so a random pick can outscore them.</s> <s>The gap exposes how sounding right quietly diverges from being right, a useful antidote to the hype.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India has launched its first hydrogen-powered passenger train, running from Jind to Sonepat and emitting only water.</s> <s>The fuel-cell train could decarbonize routes too lightly used for overhead electrification, but hydrogen rail is only as clean as its hydrogen, and most is still made from fossil gas.</s> <s>Indian Railways calls it a foundation, though the climate payoff depends entirely on where that hydrogen comes from.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>American regulators have cleared Reflect Orbital's first launch, a constellation of mirrors designed to beam reflected sunlight down to solar farms after dark.</s> <s>The <sub alias="F C C">FCC</sub> approved it over astronomers' objections, and the night sky, a shared scientific and cultural resource, has no owner to defend it.</s> <s>The question is who gets to decide the sky can be lit up for private gain.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>